# The lookup sets that hold the compound halves, by the names the language's
# .sets file gives them. A word with a capital inside it whose two parts
# these recognise is a compound written with a capital at the join, and is
# left whole for the rules rather than read as two words: SoundCloud is said
# as one word stressed as a compound, as soundcloud is.
#
# The rules say man and men weak at the end of a compound, as fireman and
# postman are said, but a name that writes Man with a capital means the
# word: SpiderMan, AntMan. A capital before a weak half is still a cut.
#
# After a prefix in nonlex_prefixes the rules stress the root, as in
# photographic, but a name that writes the prefix as its own word means it
# to be stressed: BioWare, PhotoScape. A capital after one is still a cut.
# tools/module/builtindict.py reads it.

first initial_compound_word
last final_compound_word
never not_compound
weak man men
prefixes nonlex_prefixes
